# CityEcho file ownership. scripts/check_owners.py (the git pre-commit hook) enforces this file.
#
# Format: <pattern>  <owner>     owner = A | B | C | SHARED
#   A = 📱 Mobile (citizens)   B = 🖥️ Web admin (city)   C = 📡 Sensors and data
#   SHARED = frozen shared file: changes only with CITYECHO_SHARED=1, in a commit of its own
# Patterns: ** = any subfolders, * = any name within one folder.
# The FIRST matching line wins, so specific patterns come before general ones.
# A new file that matches no line is blocked: add it here first (in a SHARED commit).

# --- Shared, frozen (every change is announced in the group, made by one person, pushed at once) ---
